# ==============================================================================
# Ukraine conflict mortality pipeline - files excluded from version control
# ==============================================================================
#
# WHAT IS AND IS NOT TRACKED
#
# Tracked:   all code, all SMALL inputs, every cached .rds extract and
#            every .rds result in data_inter/, and the figures.
#
# Not tracked: the large raw sources below, and the simulation draws.
#
# This works because every script that touches a large raw file writes a
# small cached extract into data_inter/ first (see cache_rds() in
# code/00_setup.R). Those extracts ARE tracked, so a fresh clone can run the
# whole pipeline without downloading a single one of the big files.
#
# The one exception is the simulation draws (n_sim in code/00_setup.R; 20,000
# for the reported estimates), which are too large to track and are
# regenerated by running code/11 (about half an hour at 20,000).
#
# See data_input/README.md for where to download the raw sources.
# ==============================================================================

data_deprecated/

# --- UCDP georeferenced event data (259 MB; v25_1.csv alone is over the
#     GitHub 100 MB hard limit). Cached as data_inter/ucdp_ged_events_slim.rds
data_input/ucdp/*.csv

# --- WPP 2024 fertility workbook (78 MB).
#     Cached as data_inter/ukr_asfr_wpp_2022_2025.rds
data_input/WPP2024_*.xlsx
data_input/WPP2024_*.csv.gz

# --- ualosses personnel registers (27-46 MB each).
#     These hold INDIVIDUAL-LEVEL personal data (names, dates of birth) and
#     must not be published. Everything the pipeline needs is cached as
#     anonymous aggregate counts in data_inter/ualosses_*.rds
data_input/260514_UKR_ualosses_Personnel.xlsx
data_input/ualosses_hubert_datasets/

# --- individual-level extracts of the registers, from the multistate
#     analysis (09_..._improved, 09d, 09f, 09g): one row per person or per
#     person-interval, or a model object that stores those rows. Not aggregate
#     counts, so never tracked; they are rebuilt from the registers.
data_inter/ukr_ualosses_person_trajectories.rds
data_inter/ukr_ualosses_pooled_transitions.rds
data_inter/ukr_ualosses_intervals_countingprocess.rds
data_inter/ukr_ualosses_mstate_model.rds
data_inter/ukr_ualosses_traj_mstate_model.rds

# --- simulation draws: 808 rows per draw (16 million at 20,000), regenerated
#     by code/11
data_inter/ukr_sim_draws_2022_2025*.rds
data_inter/*.fst

# --- UNICEF export: every iteration, hundreds of MB.
#     Regenerated by code/a01 from the draws.
data_inter/unicef/

# --- a separate project that happens to live under code/: 521 files, 39 MB
#     of Facebook mobility geopackages. No pipeline script references it.
code/pdr_leisure/

# --- retired inputs, outputs and scripts
data_deprecated/
_backup_removed_data/
figures/deprecated/

# --- internal team documents and correspondence, not published
review_response_*.md
review_response_*.docx

# --- R / RStudio session files
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj.user

# --- no longer read by any step. The SSSU-vs-life-table rate comparison in
#     01 that used it was retired because nothing consumed its output.
#     Kept on disk, out of the repository.
data_input/LifeTables.xlsx

# --- documentation: the methodology reports, the notes for coauthors and
#     the draft of the paper are kept on this machine, not published
documents/
